WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.570
Your money record, your story and your next 90 days.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.120
This is the video for module four of Managing Money in Daily Life.

3
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:17.780
Your final project is not a test of how much money you have. It is proof that you can see, understand and change your own daily money.

4
00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:25.450
A 1,500 naira a week improvement that is true is worth far more than a perfect record that is not.

5
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:35.930
Part A is your two-week spending record, with daily and category totals. Part B is a one-page report on one spending pattern you changed.

6
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:43.180
Part C is your progress table with the five weekly measures. Part D is your 90-day plan.

7
00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:52.340
Gather all your daily notes for the two weeks. Check every entry has a category. Put anything unclear in unknown rather than guessing.

8
00:00:53.590 --> 00:01:03.640
Check your digital spending against your bank and wallet statements for the same dates. Then total each day and each category, and make sure both add up to the same figure.

9
00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:17.730
Before you photograph or upload anything, hide your account numbers, card numbers, BVN and transaction references. Your categories and amounts are enough. Never upload a full bank statement.

10
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.380
Use five short headings: the pattern, the evidence, the rule, the result, and what you learned.

11
00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:35.380
Esther's pattern was extra keke and okada rides, because she bought baking ingredients on different days. Her record showed 9 of 22 rides were ingredient trips.

12
00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:42.490
Her evidence: in weeks 1 and 2, transport averaged 7,200 naira a week.

13
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:52.320
Her rule: buy all ingredients in one trip each Saturday with a written list. In weeks 3 and 4, transport averaged 5,000.

14
00:01:53.570 --> 00:02:04.660
She saved 2,200 naira a week, about 8,800 over four weeks, and moved it to her buffer. That is about 31 percent of her transport spending.

15
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:11.540
If your change did not work, report it honestly anyway, and say what you will try next. That shows learning.

16
00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:21.920
Money habits rarely change in one person alone. But people switch off when they feel judged. Saying 'you people waste money' starts an argument.

17
00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:34.990
Instead, share your own result with a real number. For example: I found I was spending about 2,000 naira a week on extra rides, and planning one trip on Saturday fixed most of it.

18
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:43.710
Choose a calm moment, not the day a bill is overdue. Start with what is going well, then show one number that needs help.

19
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.690
Ask for ideas before giving yours. Agree one action, and who will do it.

20
00:02:50.940 --> 00:03:00.710
Agree when you will look at the number again. In a group, never ask anyone to say their income or debts aloud, and never share someone's figures without permission.

21
00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:11.520
Choose your next goal from your weakest measure. Amina covers only 2 days, so her goal is 14 days covered in 90 days, which is about 13 weeks.

22
00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:22.290
Her target buffer is 14 times 4,000, which is 56,000 naira. She already has 8,000, so she needs 48,000 more.

23
00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:36.380
48,000 over 13 weeks is about 3,700 naira a week. It comes from 2,200 she already saves on transport, and 1,500 from cutting wants.

24
00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:46.820
She sets checkpoints at week 4, week 8 and week 13. If she falls behind, she lowers the target or finds one more leak. She does not abandon the plan.

25
00:03:48.070 --> 00:04:03.470
To remember. Honest records beat perfect-looking ones. Write your report with the pattern, evidence, rule and result. Hide private details. Share your own result kindly. And turn your next goal into a weekly amount with checkpoints.

26
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:14.090
Now assemble your project folder, hold one calm money conversation, write your 90-day plan with three checkpoints, and complete the final quiz.

27
00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.380
Continue with the lessons below.
